FINAL_SOURCE_ROLE_REFINEMENTS = {'bukhari:2709': {'report_type': 'companion_debt_payment_report_with_distinct_finite_transmitted_additions', 'speaker': 'Jabir gives the debt-payment encounter; Abu Bakr and Umar give the supplied joint reply; the explicit thirty-wasq clause remains a qualified transmitted addition.', 'reason': 'Keep the this-year fruit domain, notify-me command, unresolved seven/six alternatives, actual replies and the finite thirty-wasq debt addition. The lexical drying-place definition, pure routes, omission comparisons and nominal Asr-attendance/Dhuhr mentions remain complete source context. Do not supply an arrival predicate or harmonize the times and amounts.', 'refinement': 'The initial note treated the Asr/attendance mention as a finite variant. The exact appended wording only describes what a version mentions and supplies no own arrival predicate; it is now complete transmission context. The actual thirty-wasq father-debt clause and every other selected span remain unchanged.', 'annotation': 'The main account gives Maghrib. The appended nominal Asr-attendance mention and bare Dhuhr-prayer mention remain complete transmission context, with no time harmonization or supplied arrival predicate. The source-supplied thirty-wasq debt addition and six/seven alternatives remain literal.'}, 'bukhari:2718': {'report_type': 'companion_camel_sale_report_and_multiple_qualified_finite_transmitted_variants', 'speaker': 'Jabir reports the main encounter; each retained finite version keeps its own printed transmission framing. The four-uqiya uncertainty has an unnamed first-person voice.', 'reason': 'Preserve every finite purchase, riding condition, temporal scope, speech predicate, retained-price fact and the full material quantity uncertainty. The one-uqiya-of-gold and two-hundred-dirham clauses are nominal version descriptions and remain transmission context, alongside pure routes, corroboration pointers, currency conversion, omission comparison and compiler preference. Do not choose a price or invent another sale.', 'refinement': 'The initial note over-weighted the attribution of the gold and two-hundred-dirham labels. Their actual role is to describe a version, without the purchase predicate supplied by other retained variants. Only those two complete selected labels per language move to source context. Every finite purchase, riding condition and the full I-think four-uqiya uncertainty retain their exact original component identities.', 'annotation': 'Retained finite variants contain differing purchase amounts and conditions, including the unresolved four-uqiya wording. The gold and two-hundred-dirham nominal labels remain complete transmission context; the final compiler preference also stays context. No amount, route or transaction is harmonized.'}, 'bukhari:2737': {'report_type': 'companion_endowment_consultation_and_actual_stipulations_report', 'speaker': 'Ibn Umar reports Umar consultation and actual endowment stipulations in two same-family components.', 'reason': 'Keep the conditional advice, Umar actual stipulations, every beneficiary and all trustee-use limits. The prefatory route, waqf synonym and appended Ibn Awn/Ibn Sirin explanation remain complete source context. The named reception frame establishes the appendix attribution but its function is to interpret the cited stewardship rule, rather than supply another underlying report body.', 'refinement': 'The immutable initial note treated the named Ibn Awn/Ibn Sirin reply as a report component. On exact source-role review, that tail expressly explains the preceding hadith steward rule when the hadith is mentioned; it is retained as attributed side explanation. This is not a general exclusion of Successor sayings, legal content or named encounters. Both complete Umar/Ibn Umar report components and all trustee conditions remain unchanged.', 'annotation': 'The entire appended Ibn Awn/Ibn Sirin exchange is retained as attributed interpretive context. Its named voice is preserved without promoting the explanatory restriction into the underlying Umar report. The original words, beneficiaries and trustee conditions are unchanged.'}, 'bukhari:2763': {'report_type': 'companion_attributed_verse_interpretations_and_historical_report', 'speaker': 'Urwah frames Aisha actual responses, quoted verse subjects and historical statement in three same-family components.', 'reason': 'Keep both supplied verse excerpts and renderings as subjects of Aisha actual interpretation, her attributed historical statement and every conditional, actor and family scope. The final narrator-said comparison is an appended legal explanation and remains complete source context, alongside the pure earlier route. No recitation event, verse completion or unnamed-speaker identity is invented.', 'refinement': 'The initial note admitted the final narrator-labelled comparison as an anonymous interpretive saying. On exact source-role review it functions as an appended explanation after the actual Urwah/Aisha exchange, so that whole tail remains source context. The distinction concerns explanatory role, not legal subject matter or anonymous attribution alone. Aisha three components, actual verses/renderings and all meaningful predicates and conditions remain exact.', 'annotation': 'The final narrator-said comparison remains complete attributed explanatory context; the source does not identify that narrator. All preceding actual Aisha responses, verse words/renderings and necessary conditional predicates retain their own source text and speaker distinctions.'}}
